Yes, it is possible to save an image to your computer from a React app if you only have the image's URL. You can achieve this by using JavaScript's `fetch` API to download the image and then use the HTML5 `download` attribute to prompt the user to save it.

Here's an example implementation:

```javascript
const saveImageToComputer = (imageUrl) => {
  fetch(imageUrl)
    .then(response => response.blob())
    .then(blob => {
      const url = URL.createObjectURL(blob);
      const link = document.createElement('a');
      link.href = url;
      link.setAttribute('download', 'image.png');
      link.click();
      URL.revokeObjectURL(url);
    });
}
```

In this example, the `saveImageToComputer` function takes the image URL as an argument and performs the following steps:

1. Fetches the image using `fetch`.
2. Converts the fetched response into a `Blob` object.
