4. Creates a dummy `<a>` element with the URL and sets the `download` attribute to specify the desired file name (`image.png` in this example).
5. Triggers a click event programmatically on the `<a>` element to prompt the user to save the image.
6. Revokes the URL object to clean up.

You can call this `saveImageToComputer` function with the desired image URL whenever you want to trigger the image download.

