To update multiple files, you can make the following changes to your code:

1. Update the `uploadImage` method in the `CloudinaryService` class to accept an array of files:

```typescript
async uploadImage(
  files: Express.Multer.File[],
): Promise<(UploadApiResponse | UploadApiErrorResponse)[]> {
  return Promise.all(
    files.map((file) => {
      return new Promise((resolve, reject) => {
        const upload = v2.uploader.upload_stream((error, result) => {
          if (error) return reject(error);
          resolve(result);
        });
        toStream(file.buffer).pipe(upload);
      });
    }),
  );
}
```

2. Update the `uploadImage` method in the `CloudinaryController` class to accept an array of files:
```typescript
@Post()
@UseInterceptors(FileInterceptor('image', { limits: { files: 10 } }))
async uploadImages(@UploadedFiles() files: Express.Multer.File[]) {
  const uploadStreams: any[] = await this.cloudinaryService.uploadImage(files);

  return uploadStreams;
}
```

